  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 226 PM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nUpper ridging continues over the Rockies and Plains, with some\nweak embedded shortwaves coming over top of the ridge today and\ntomorrow. The higher heights will push further north on\nWednesday, ahead of a stronger shortwave coming over top of the\nridge on Thursday. After a brief period of northwesterly flow,\nupper ridging builds back into the region for the weekend. Many\nof the ensemble members have a stronger trough starting to track\nalong the international border on Monday, bringing us\nsouthwesterly flow aloft. However, a cluster of around 35 \npercent of the long range ensemble members keep the 588dm meter \nnosing up into ND and the troughing much less impressive. At\nthis point, a more active pattern and cooler temperatures look\nlike they will at least hold off until next week.\n\n...Heat wave continuing and rain chances mid-week...\n\nOne of the weak embedded shortwaves coming over the top of the\nridge has started to produce some showers and thunderstorms in\nor near north central ND. SPC meso page has decent 1000 to 1500\nJ/kg of ML CAPE and shear around 40 kts, but with very weak\nforcing, and extremely warm mid-level temps, the cells that are\ndeveloping are struggling. CAMs have that trend continuing with\nthe next weak shortwave arriving later this evening, and this \nseems reasonable. Our northwestern counties could see a few \nsprinkles this afternoon and evening, but substantial\nprecipitation will hold off until Wednesday/Thursday as NBM \nprobabilities of at least a tenth of an inch of rain finally \nrise above 50 percent. ECMWF EFI continues to show a signal for\nheat continuing through the weekend, and NBM probabilities for\ntemperatures over 95 degrees are over 70 percent for Wednesday.\nLikely will need heat headlines of some sort again Wednesday so\nwill continue to monitor.",
